From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TheDBP <TheDBP@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 22:04:03 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] ether: let the ACDB calibration paths be set, and say where
 WFC provisioning lives

vendor_init is refused audio_prop, so the seven persist.audio.calfile* paths init.qcom.rc sets from
this device's own ACDB data all read back empty and the audio HAL has been running on generic
calibration since the port began:

    avc: denied { set } for property=persist.audio.calfile0 scontext=u:r:vendor_init:s0
                                                            tcontext=u:object_r:audio_prop:s0

AOSP folded the exported_audio_prop type vendor_init used to hold back into audio_prop, so vendor rc
files written against the old world stopped working silently. public/vendor_init.te already grants
vendor_init a long list of other core property types and there is no neverallow against this one.

Found by sweeping property *set* denials, which name the property where read denials do not.

The carrier config gains only a comment. Wi-Fi calling needs IMS provisioning required for VOICE
over IWLAN, and that cannot be expressed here: it needs a nested <pbundle_as_map>, and this file is
parsed by PersistableBundle.restoreFromXml() with throwException=false, so a nested bundle it cannot
handle is dropped in silence. The XML compiles into the APK correctly, verified with aapt2, and
simply never reaches the merged config while every scalar around it applies. The setting lives in
frameworks/base as the default for Ims.KEY_MMTEL_REQUIRES_PROVISIONING_BUNDLE; the comment says so,
so the next reader does not add it back here.
---
 .../packages/apps/CarrierConfig/res/xml/vendor.xml    | 11 +++++++++++
 sepolicy/vendor_init.te                               | 11 +++++++++++
 2 files changed, 22 insertions(+)

diff --git a/overlay/packages/apps/CarrierConfig/res/xml/vendor.xml b/overlay/packages/apps/CarrierConfig/res/xml/vendor.xml
index cc1f91b..46a5504 100644
--- a/overlay/packages/apps/CarrierConfig/res/xml/vendor.xml
+++ b/overlay/packages/apps/CarrierConfig/res/xml/vendor.xml
@@ -20,5 +20,16 @@
         <boolean name="carrier_volte_override_wfc_provisioning_bool" value="true" />
         <int name="carrier_default_wfc_ims_mode_int" value="1" />
         <int name="carrier_default_wfc_ims_roaming_mode_int" value="1" />
+
+        <!-- Wi-Fi calling needs IMS provisioning required for VOICE over IWLAN, or the modem is
+             never told the feature is provisioned and declines every attempt to configure it. That
+             is NOT set here, deliberately: it needs a nested <pbundle_as_map>, and this file is
+             parsed by PersistableBundle.restoreFromXml() with throwException=false, so a nested
+             bundle it cannot handle is dropped in silence. The XML compiles into the APK correctly
+             and simply never reaches the merged config; every scalar around it applies, which
+             makes it look like it worked.
+
+             It lives in frameworks/base instead, as the default for
+             Ims.KEY_MMTEL_REQUIRES_PROVISIONING_BUNDLE. See that patch. -->
     </carrier_config>
 </carrier_config_list>
diff --git a/sepolicy/vendor_init.te b/sepolicy/vendor_init.te
index 57d9d14..ec22c3b 100644
--- a/sepolicy/vendor_init.te
+++ b/sepolicy/vendor_init.te
@@ -15,3 +15,14 @@ allow vendor_init radio_data_file:file create_file_perms;
 
 # copy_complete under the radio core data dir
 allow vendor_init radio_core_data_file:file create_file_perms;
+
+# init.qcom.rc sets persist.audio.calfile0..6 to this device's own ACDB calibration
+# (NBQ_Speaker_cal.acdb, NBQ_Handset_cal.acdb, NBQ_Headset_cal.acdb and four more) and every one is
+# refused, so all seven read back empty and the audio HAL has been running on generic calibration:
+#   avc: denied { set } for property=persist.audio.calfile0 scontext=u:r:vendor_init:s0
+#                                                           tcontext=u:object_r:audio_prop:s0
+# AOSP used to grant vendor_init the separate exported_audio_prop type and folded it back into
+# audio_prop, which silently broke vendor rc files written against the old world. public/vendor_init.te
+# already grants vendor_init a long list of other core property types, and there is no neverallow
+# against this one.
+set_prop(vendor_init, audio_prop)
